WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.600
Something passes from the notochord into the neural tube.

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.360
What is it, and how does a cell receive it?

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.210
The signal got a name in December 1993.

4
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.870
Three papers appeared in one issue of the journal Cell.

5
00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:22.783
They described vertebrate relatives of hedgehog, a fly gene for a secreted signal.

6
00:00:23.643 --> 00:00:26.743
One paper was in mouse, one in zebrafish, one in chick.

7
00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:32.997
The gene, Sonic hedgehog, was expressed in notochord and floor plate, the tissues

8
00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:34.337
the grafts had pointed to.

9
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.780
In the mouse paper, forcing the gene on where it is normally absent switched on

10
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:40.780
floor-plate genes.

11
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:45.653
Next, Thomas Jessell's laboratory put the protein back into a dish.

12
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:49.453
An explant is a small piece of tissue grown in a dish.

13
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:56.373
In 1995, Henk Roelink and colleagues gave explants the purified signaling fragment

14
00:00:56.373 --> 00:00:57.373
of the protein.

15
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:02.277
At the higher concentrations tested, explants made floor-plate markers.

16
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:05.137
Lower ones gave motor neuron markers.

17
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.900
One protein, at different doses, gave different ventral fates.

18
00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:12.483
How does a cell receive it?

19
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:14.283
Think of a brake.

20
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:16.873
The receptor, Patched, is the brake.

21
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:21.633
On its own, it holds a second membrane protein, Smoothened, switched off.

22
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:25.293
Sonic hedgehog binds Patched and lifts the brake.

23
00:01:26.153 --> 00:01:28.533
Smoothened is freed, and the pathway turns on.

24
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:33.883
What changes is a family of transcription factors called the Gli proteins.

25
00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:38.993
Without the signal, Gli3 above all is cut into a short repressor.

26
00:01:39.853 --> 00:01:41.893
That step depends on the primary cilium.

27
00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:47.767
With the signal, less repressor is made, and full-length Gli acts as an activator.

28
00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:53.297
In this model, a progenitor reads the balance of activator against repressor.

29
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.590
One tool switches the pathway off.

30
00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.270
Cyclopamine, an alkaloid from a plant, blocks Smoothened.

31
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:05.553
Necessity came from a knockout, a mouse with a gene deliberately disrupted.

32
00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.607
Mice lacking Sonic hedgehog have no floor plate.

33
00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:13.047
They lack most ventral cell types of the neural tube.

34
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.530
Now a sharper test.

35
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.810
Suppose Sonic hedgehog's main job is to stop Gli3 repressor from forming.

36
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:27.980
Predict. In a mouse lacking Sonic hedgehog, what should removing Gli3 as well do to

37
00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:28.980
its ventral cells?

38
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:40.243
Removing Gli3 restores motor neurons and several ventral interneuron classes.

39
00:02:41.317 --> 00:02:44.617
Removing Gli3 did part of Sonic hedgehog's job.

40
00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:47.057
That is a double-mutant rescue.

41
00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.007
A rescue shows that two genes interact, not how.

42
00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:53.887
Here, the known pathway supplies the how.

43
00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.900
So much of what Sonic hedgehog does in the spinal cord is to block Gli3 repressor.

44
00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:04.573
The takeaway: the signal is Sonic hedgehog, read through a brake.

45
00:03:05.553 --> 00:03:07.473
Next, how does an amount become an address?
